==English==
{{was wotd|2018|November|14}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Etale de fruit en rue.jpg|thumb|A fruiterer’s [[roadside]] [[stall#Noun|stall]] in [[Senegal]]]]

From Late {{inh|en|enm|fruiterer|fruiterē̆r|fruit grower; fruit dealer}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=fruiterē̆r, n.|id=MED17848|accessdate=2 May 2018}}</ref> from {{m|enm|fruiter|fruitē̆r|fruit dealer; household official having charge of fruit}}<ref name="MED">{{R:MED Online|entry=fruitē̆r, n.|id=MED17847|accessdate=2 May 2018}}</ref> {{suffix|en||er}} (it is unclear why the second suffix was added).<ref>{{R:Oxford Dictionaries Online}}</ref> ''Fruitē̆r'' is derived from {{der|en|xno|fruitier}} or {{der|en|fr|fruitier||fruit-seller}},<ref name="MED"/> from {{m|fr|fruit||fruit}} (from {{der|en|la|frū̆ctus||produce, product, fruit; enjoyment, satisfaction}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰruHg-||to have enjoyment of; make use of}}) + {{m|fr|-ier||''suffix forming names of jobs''}}.

